The public beach in the centre of Flic en Flac is where the village comes to the sea. Filao trees give shade along the sand and the reef keeps the lagoon calm and shallow. In the evening the sun sets straight into the Indian Ocean.

At weekends and on public holidays it fills with Mauritian families and picnics and music and it is lively and friendly. On weekdays and early in the morning it is much quieter.

## Good to know

- Food stalls and snack vans are usually found near the car park.
- For more space walk south along the sand towards Wolmar.
